# name: test/sql/integration/protocol_version/version_mismatch.test
# description: VGI application protocol_version mismatch is fatal at the dispatch boundary
# group: [vgi_integration_protocol_version]

# The fixture worker declares a protocol_version outside the extension's
# supported window. ATTACH negotiates first (docs/protocol_versions.md): over a
# byte transport the worker's reflection answer names its version, over HTTP
# its refusal of catalog_attach does. Either way the ranges are disjoint, so
# ATTACH fails with the protocol_version_unsupported error naming both. This
# guards the rolling-upgrade boundary: a worker outside the window cannot
# silently omit records the extension expects.
#
# Provisioned via the VGI_BAD_PROTOCOL_WORKER fixture
# (vgi-fixture-bad-protocol-worker) — see vgi-python/vgi/_test_fixtures/bad_protocol.py.

require-env VGI_BAD_PROTOCOL_WORKER

require vgi

require httpfs

# The mismatch is detected on the first dispatched request, which ATTACH makes
# during catalog discovery — so ATTACH itself fails.
statement error
ATTACH 'badproto' AS badproto (TYPE vgi, LOCATION '${VGI_BAD_PROTOCOL_WORKER}');
----
<REGEX>:.*protocol_version_unsupported: the VGI worker supports vgi\.v3 \d+\.\d+-\d+\.\d+; this vgi extension supports vgi\.v3 \d+\.\d+-\d+\.\d+\..*
